From: WinBoat
Subject: [PATCH] venus: yield before sleeping in waits on Windows

Venus waits for fences, semaphores and queries by polling (vn_relax): a few
yields, then sleeps of 160 us, 320 us and so on. On Windows a sleep lasts at
least one period of the timer interrupt, 0.5 ms at best (high-resolution
waitable timers included), where an empty submission's round trip through
the host takes ~70 us: every wait that didn't finish within the yields cost
~0.5 ms. vkd3d-proton waits like that on each fence, so a D3D12
ExecuteCommandLists + Signal + wait took ~575 us.

On Windows vn_relax now yields for up to 0.5 ms before its first sleep. The
iteration count, which paces the sleeps and the watchdog (warning and alive
checks), only starts counting after that, so both behave as before.

Measured in a Windows 11 guest (RTX 3080 host): an empty vkQueueSubmit +
vkWaitSemaphores 537 -> 70 us, vkd3d-proton submit + fence wait 575 -> 94 us.
---
diff --git a/src/util/os_time.c b/src/util/os_time.c
--- a/src/util/os_time.c
+++ b/src/util/os_time.c
@@ -79,7 +79,8 @@
       return;
    /* Sleep() lasts at least one tick of the system timer, 15.6 ms unless some process raised its resolution: a
     * wait that polls with short sleeps (Venus' vn_relax starts at 160 us) then waits a whole tick each time. A
-    * high-resolution waitable timer (Windows 10 1803 and later) sleeps for the time asked.
+    * high-resolution waitable timer (Windows 10 1803 and later) sleeps for the time asked, rounded up to the
+    * finest timer interrupt period (0.5 ms).
     */
 #ifndef CREATE_WAITABLE_TIMER_HIGH_RESOLUTION
 #define CREATE_WAITABLE_TIMER_HIGH_RESOLUTION 0x00000002
diff --git a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_common.c b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_common.c
--- a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_common.c
+++ b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_common.c
@@ -253,6 +253,20 @@
    const uint32_t warn_order = state->profile.warn_order;
    const uint32_t abort_order = state->profile.abort_order;
 
+#if DETECT_OS_WINDOWS
+   /* WinBoat: a sleep lasts at least a tick of the timer interrupt, 0.5 ms at best (high-resolution timers too),
+    * where a GPU round trip through the host takes ~70 us. Yield for up to a tick before the first sleep; the
+    * iterations, which pace the sleeps and the watchdog, only count from then on.
+    */
+   const int64_t now_ns = os_time_get_nano();
+   if (!state->spin_end_ns)
+      state->spin_end_ns = now_ns + 500000;
+   if (now_ns < state->spin_end_ns) {
+      thrd_yield();
+      return;
+   }
+#endif
+
    uint32_t *iter = &state->iter;
    (*iter)++;
    if (*iter < (1 << busy_wait_order)) {
diff --git a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_common.h b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_common.h
--- a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_common.h
+++ b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_common.h
@@ -266,6 +266,8 @@
    uint32_t iter;
    const struct vn_relax_profile profile;
    const char *reason_str;
+   /* WinBoat: when the Windows spin of vn_relax ends (0 before the first call) */
+   int64_t spin_end_ns;
 };
 
